WEBVTT

1
00:00:12.534 --> 00:00:17.136
Zann landed in a puddle of swampy water. "Drat," he muttered.

2
00:00:17.137 --> 00:00:21.051
His Conveyance teacher was always scolding him for this sort of thing.

3
00:00:21.052 --> 00:00:24.842
Being a Red, Zann could zap himself far—and fast.

4
00:00:24.843 --> 00:00:27.250
But his focus still needed some work.

5
00:00:27.251 --> 00:00:32.003
That didn't matter now though. He was out of the house. It was time to find Darb.

6
00:00:32.004 --> 00:00:37.606
Pursing his lips, he whistled, trying to imitate the call of a lesser swamp swift.

7
00:00:37.607 --> 00:00:41.697
"Not bad," a voice said from the grassy hillock behind him.

8
00:00:41.698 --> 00:00:44.382
"I always knew you had talents other than magic."

9
00:00:44.383 --> 00:00:49.320
Zann spun around and grinned. "Hey, Darb," he said, stepping out of the water.

10
00:00:49.321 --> 00:00:52.772
"Sorry I'm late. Boz didn't want me to go out."

11
00:00:52.773 --> 00:00:58.934
"Because of the warning about Reds disappearing?" Darb asked thoughtfully. "I've been hearing about that."

12
00:00:58.935 --> 00:01:04.673
Darb was a Void, one of a small group of people in Magica born without any magical abilities.

13
00:01:04.674 --> 00:01:07.707
That was the reason he and Zann had met in the first place.

14
00:01:07.708 --> 00:01:15.324
On Zann's first day at the Swamp Bottom School, he'd encountered Jev and his friends teasing Darb. Zann had told them to stop.

15
00:01:15.325 --> 00:01:18.511
"Who's going to make me?" Jev had sneered.

16
00:01:18.512 --> 00:01:22.343
"That red hair of yours doesn't mean you get to tell me what to do."

17
00:01:22.344 --> 00:01:25.837
Then he'd turned and shoved Darb into the wall—hard.

18
00:01:25.838 --> 00:01:29.804
Looking back, Zann knew he probably should have called a teacher.

19
00:01:29.805 --> 00:01:35.561
Instead he'd acted on impulse, rubbing his fingers together until sparks began to jump from his hand.

20
00:01:35.562 --> 00:01:40.794
Jev didn’t even know what had happened until his friends started snickering and pointing at him.

21
00:01:40.795 --> 00:01:44.260
Zann had given him a pair of oversized donkey ears.

22
00:01:44.261 --> 00:01:47.196
It took Jev several tries to undo the spell.

23
00:01:47.197 --> 00:01:52.204
Ever since then Jev had been Zann's enemy, and Darb had been Zann's friend.

24
00:01:52.205 --> 00:01:58.430
Darb didn't attend school anymore. Voids were only required to study the basics of theory and history.

25
00:01:58.431 --> 00:02:04.478
Once classes started doing practical magic lessons, Voids usually dropped out and studied on their own.

26
00:02:04.479 --> 00:02:13.039
Most ended up finding careers as companions, greeters, animal caretakers, and mediators, or other jobs that required no magic.

27
00:02:13.040 --> 00:02:17.558
Most people in Magica would never purposely discriminate against a Void.

28
00:02:17.559 --> 00:02:22.335
But Zann had noticed that people said things in front of Darb that they wouldn't say in front of others.

29
00:02:22.336 --> 00:02:26.824
It was as if they thought Voids were deaf and dumb as well as lacking magic.

30
00:02:26.825 --> 00:02:31.772
That didn't seem fair to Zann. But it did allow Darb to hear a lot of interesting gossip.

31
00:02:31.773 --> 00:02:35.412
"What have you heard about the warning?" Zann asked his friend now.

32
00:02:35.413 --> 00:02:40.302
"Not much," Darb said. "Everyone's talking about the message from the palace though.

33
00:02:40.303 --> 00:02:45.551
The mayor is so nervous that she put a Shield spell over the entire town hall."

34
00:02:45.552 --> 00:02:47.908
"Boz is trying to find out more.

35
00:02:47.909 --> 00:02:53.083
In the meantime he wants me to stay inside." Zann rolled his eyes.

36
00:02:53.084 --> 00:02:56.914
"You can't blame him for being worried after what happened to your parents."

37
00:02:56.915 --> 00:03:02.350
"I guess." Zann jumped onto a larger hillock. "So what have you been doing?"

38
00:03:02.351 --> 00:03:04.172
"Studying insects."

39
00:03:04.173 --> 00:03:10.598
"Insects, huh?" Zann said. "Why not study something more exciting? Dragons, maybe?"

40
00:03:10.599 --> 00:03:14.517
"Speaking of dragons, where's Zing?" Darb asked.

41
00:03:14.518 --> 00:03:18.934
"He was outside when I left. I couldn't get him without Boz seeing me."

42
00:03:18.935 --> 00:03:24.159
Darb looked disappointed. Everyone assumed he'd end up being an animal caretaker someday.

43
00:03:24.160 --> 00:03:27.014
He loved animals of all kinds, and they loved him.

44
00:03:27.015 --> 00:03:30.779
Zing broke into a happy whistling song whenever he saw him.

45
00:03:30.780 --> 00:03:35.137
Darb stepped toward a slow-moving stream. "Look, panic bugs."

46
00:03:35.138 --> 00:03:39.471
He leaned closer for a better look. "Can you get a picture of them for me?"

47
00:03:39.472 --> 00:03:44.007
"Sure." Zann rubbed his hands together and stared at the shiny red bugs.

48
00:03:44.008 --> 00:03:45.010
Blink!

49
00:03:45.011 --> 00:03:48.220
A piece of paper appeared and fluttered to the swampy ground.

50
00:03:48.221 --> 00:03:52.853
Zann picked it up. The image of the panic bugs was there in full color.

51
00:03:52.854 --> 00:03:57.679
"Thanks." Darb took the blink image, folded it, and put it into his pocket.

52
00:03:57.680 --> 00:04:04.900
Then he gently scooped up the bugs and put them in his other pocket, being careful not to startle them into releasing their stink.

53
00:04:04.901 --> 00:04:09.606
"Want to help me look for leeches?" he asked. "I've seen them around here before."

54
00:04:09.607 --> 00:04:13.033
"Leeches?" Zann echoed. "Why?"

55
00:04:13.034 --> 00:04:18.228
"I've been reading about them. It's fascinating how they can suck the magic out of people."

56
00:04:18.229 --> 00:04:25.520
"Yeah." Zann grinned. "Back in First City, my friends and I used to stick them on each other as a joke.

57
00:04:25.521 --> 00:04:31.528
It would take about a million of them to drain enough magic to make a difference, but it was still funny."

58
00:04:31.529 --> 00:04:37.102
Darb peered into the water's murky depths. "Leeches are very shy," he said.

59
00:04:37.103 --> 00:04:39.358
"They live at the bottom of streams like this.

60
00:04:39.359 --> 00:04:42.282
We'll have to be quiet and feel around in the water."

61
00:04:42.283 --> 00:04:46.225
"Why go to all that trouble?" Zann rubbed his fingers together.

62
00:04:46.226 --> 00:04:51.142
"I'll displace the water. Then you can grab as many leeches as you want."

63
00:04:51.143 --> 00:04:54.297
"Zann, wait!" Darb began. "That won't—"

64
00:04:54.298 --> 00:04:55.535
Shloop!

65
00:04:55.536 --> 00:05:00.495
The water in the nearest section of the stream levitated, hanging as droplets in the air.

66
00:05:00.496 --> 00:05:05.885
Several fish and other creatures were left lying on the bottom of the streambed, looking confused.

67
00:05:05.886 --> 00:05:16.126
"Leeches!" Zann cried, pointing. Almost before he spotted them, the slimy little creatures had burrowed into the soft sand. "Oh. They're gone."

68
00:05:16.127 --> 00:05:20.020
"I tried to tell you that," Darb said with a sigh.

69
00:05:20.021 --> 00:05:23.500
"They dive away from air unless they're latched on to someone."

70
00:05:23.501 --> 00:05:28.245
"Sorry," Zann said. "Hey, did you hear that?"

71
00:05:28.246 --> 00:05:29.568
"Hear what?"

72
00:05:29.569 --> 00:05:34.201
Zann tilted his head, listening. "That buzzing noise," he said.

73
00:05:34.202 --> 00:05:39.417
"Sounds like an irritated spy fly, or maybe—"

74
00:05:39.418 --> 00:05:43.039
A loud, angry buzzing drowned out his words.

75
00:05:43.040 --> 00:05:52.036
Suddenly a whole swarm of tiny, glittering dragons came zipping out of a hole in the bank and started stinging him!
